member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T07:34:04-07:00","id":1262134,"title":"","content":"Scion: Hero references a &quot;Black pool&quot; which I think is supposed to be the pool of Momentum? I was not able to find a definition to this anywhere else in either Origin or in Hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24718-many-meats","name":"Many Meats","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T08:15:25-07:00","id":1262148,"title":"","content":"Page 249 under Epic Strength- &quot;You can use strength in place of presence for intimidation...&quot;<br /> Replace strength with Might","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T10:40:33-07:00","id":1262182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261334-errata-scion-hero?p=1261688#post1261688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s errata: the text suggests two names and only lists one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't correct Rich. Rich's word is final.<br /> <br /> Errata is addressed to us. If you're talking to each other, then you're having a discussion, and it should go elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T11:44:07-07:00","id":1262191,"title":"","content":"Very well, then:<br /> <br /> P.95: \u201cBast wars with herself over her own nature, even in the modern World. When she is calm and con-templative, she goes by Bast, the prophet and gentle guide. When visions of the future become too much, the old warrior surfaces within her.\u201c The text suggests Bast is one of two names, but never gives another. The writeup for Bast also lists Sekhmet as an alias, then says on the next page in a sidebar that the two are not the same goddess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T13:01:38-07:00","id":1262205,"title":"","content":"Page 253, the Divination Boon: &quot;A character\u2019s good luck runs once this benefit has&quot; <br /> <br /> I think there should be an <i>out</i> in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T20:25:11-07:00","id":1262281,"title":"","content":"p. 178: Second paragraph: &quot;She prays every day, stars at statues...&quot; should be &quot;She prays every day, stares at statues...&quot;<br /> <br /> The last sentence in the second paragraph is awkward, almost like it has an extra &quot;and&quot; in it. It should probably be split, perhaps as &quot;...and a card tied to a brimming-over bank account; they also blessed the weapons she's always had.&quot;<br /> <br /> And finally, the last sentence in the paragraph is incomplete. It ends with &quot;Her father spoke to her through&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23872-doryna","user":"Doryna","date":". 10-22-2018, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23872-doryna","name":"Doryna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23872_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T20:41:39-07:00","id":1262285,"title":"","content":"Unsure if it's planned to change but the Character sheet is missing some key things. On the example heroes, they're either not listed or put in strange places. There's no spot for Legendary Title (missing from all characters) and there's no spot for Birthrights (put under Path Effects for the pregens).<br /> <br /> Rashmi is also missing asterisks on two of her attributes (Might and Presence) and her Mental attributes are one dot short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12919-mystrich","user":"Mystrich","date":". 10-22-2018, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12919-mystrich","name":"Mystrich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T21:14:17-07:00","id":1262287,"title":"","content":"Captain of Industry and Inspirational Aura, under Heroic Leader Knacks, are duplicates of one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T01:28:21-07:00","id":1262316,"title":"","content":"Page 20, first paragraph, Tsukiyomi is called the \u201cmood god\u201d instead of \u201cMoon god\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T04:53:23-07:00","id":1262328,"title":"","content":"Page 169: toward the end of the page - a letter in the name Omolara Mu_ammad is missing<br /> Page 268: in the story about Dodaem - The other Scions express doubt for the Scion of the Manitou by scoffing at him. Why would they do this in a World wear all myths are true? Seems like prejudice against the beliefs/powers of the Manitou.<br /> Page 297: Primary Pool for Kerberos Hounds - &quot;Being a Good Boy&quot; should be &quot;Being a Good Dog&quot;. There's nothing else in the write up to suggest that all Kerberos Hounds are boys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T05:16:30-07:00","id":1262335,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Netjer's Pantheon path skills<br /> <br /> Hero Page 104: Path Skills: Academics, Occult<br /> <br /> Origin Page 172: Asset Skills: Academics, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Not sure which is correct but they should be aligned.<br /> <br /> Same for Manitou<br /> SH 93 Asset Skills: Athletics, Persuasion<br /> SO 171 Path Skills: Medicine, Occult<br /> <br /> May be the same on more but I have not checked yet - Will post if I spot more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T05:42:25-07:00","id":1262339,"title":"","content":"Regarding upgrading a Origin character to Hero, it looks like the option in origin to take 2 additional knacks is RAW far worse than taking 4 points of birthrights if you know your game will move to Hero.<br /> <br /> As hero states on page 171 your Knacks cap at owning 5, so if I have brought the extra 2 I only gain 2 more. But this isn't the same for Birthrights at 7, it doesn't say that is a cap.<br /> <br /> Does this mean I can buy 4 dots of birthrights at the Origin level, then get an extra 7 when I hit hero for a total of 11? This also seems like a problem for a protracted Origin game, buying knacks is at a serious disadvantage if the XP you spend on them is ignored when hitting Hero as you level up to 5 knacks anyway, but your allies who brought Birthrights just get more and can match you on knacks.<br /> <br /> It feels like it should be gain 4 new Knacks and 7 birthrights - but without the limit that is put on knacks, instead just the limit of 5 active knacks at once.<br /> <br /> Troubled line to remove/ reword &quot;If your pre-Visitation Scion already knows more than five Knacks, don\u2019t purchase any more; otherwise, bring the total known to five&quot; Reword to align with how you gain extra knacks for the extra callings at Hero Level","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T07:52:52-07:00","id":1262357,"title":"","content":"on the table of contents, Centaur is made to be under Satyr and on 313 the Centaur heading isn't on the same size as when the begin to talk about the other deziens","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T08:20:20-07:00","id":1262362,"title":"","content":"312.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">The Hulder Path contacts are larger then the rest of the text</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T14:40:18-07:00","id":1262416,"title":"","content":"PG 315 - Therianthrope is bookmarked under wolf warrior, not its own entry. Same with Therianthrope heading size. Same issue as pointed out by Iceblade44, just another section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T14:42:33-07:00","id":1262417,"title":"","content":"The example characters starting on pg 172 and the description of callings on pg 191 state that 1 legend heroes have 5 dots of callings, but on pg 183 step 5 of character creation has a user getting 2 dots in one calling and 1 dot in the other two.<br /> &quot;Your character receives two dots in one of their Callings and one dot each in the other two.&quot;<br /> Shouldn't these descriptions match up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11249-regem_caelum","name":"Regem_Caelum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T17:42:24-07:00","id":1262442,"title":"","content":"Page 189: The Virtuous Condition and the description of what Virtues do in general are identical (&quot;Every point of Momentum ... that doesn\u2019t come out of the pool&quot;). Unless I am mistaken, these should have separate effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T20:24:38-07:00","id":1262460,"title":"","content":"Page 77, Benzaiten\u2019s purviews includes \u201cAnimal\u201d instead of \u201cBeast\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T04:28:55-07:00","id":1262495,"title":"","content":"p.259, Voice of Seven Thunders boon mentions a Spectacle stunt and benefiting from Threats (which is capitalized, suggesting it is a specific mechanical thing), but I cannot find either of these listed in Hero or Origin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T12:57:15-07:00","id":1262573,"title":"","content":"P. 178 &quot;Her father's cult has given her...a first-class airplane ticket to BWI International,...&quot; is tautologous. The &quot;I&quot; in &quot;BWI&quot; already stands for International.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12598-karasu-sama","name":"Karasu-sama","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T19:44:14-07:00","id":1262784,"title":"","content":"P 202. In &quot;Building the creature.&quot; Two p. XX","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T21:47:36-07:00","id":1263000,"title":"","content":"Page 247: The Unerring Flight boon on is listed as Cost: 1 Legend rather than either Cost: Imbue 1 Legend or Cost: Spend 1 Legend","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I'm immortal, I've been right so far&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/301-bwchism","name":"bwchism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T20:26:51-07:00","id":1263156,"title":"","content":"Scion hero errata from a backer-<br /> P15: the 3rd paragraph under the 'Titans' heading: font issue in the case of the word r\u0101k[x]a-sas. [x]=font issue<br /> P30: L3 1st column: The Grandchildren (Yoruba: [x]m[x]). [x]=font issue<br /> P172-181: page numbers missing.<br /> P 173, 312. References are made to the knack Structural Integrity. This does not appear to exist.<br /> P175: the knacks Bold Introduction and Command Voice appear to be missing.<br /> P177: the knack Healer with the Hands of a God is probably referenced as Surgeon with the Hands of a God.<br /> P185: in step 9 it is not clear whether one can buy one immortal knack with the 2 extra knack allowance. Also, in the experience table it seems that heroic and immortal knacks cost the same. Is this intended?<br /> P202: The reference to Creature examples in chapter 6 does not appear except for the basilisk and the sphinx. At any rate, no creature rating is provided in chapter 6 as promised. The table which continues on p283 does fulfil this to an extent though.<br /> P203: it is suggested that the Savage tag for followers can be given to Creatures. What is the cost in this case?<br /> P238, 244, 261: The Blinded condition referenced here does not appear to exist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-27T20:46:59-07:00","id":1263157,"title":"","content":"On page 72, Susano-o has Forge (Metallurgy)<br /> <br /> On page 75, Takemikazuchi has Sky (Thunder)<br /> <br /> RAW neither of these purviews specialize. If they\u2019re meant to be able to like this that needs a rules clarification, and probably some examples in other Pantheons. Only Artistry, Beasts, and Passion specialize like that in the Powers chapter or in the other Pantheon writeups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T11:05:56-07:00","id":1263217,"title":"","content":"The Sidebar LEGEND, RELICS, AND DENIZENS (page 311) contradicts the Character Creation rules for Legendary Denizens (pg 171)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/963-kylar","name":"Kylar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar963_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T14:18:42-07:00","id":1263255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kylar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1261334-errata-scion-hero?p=1263217#post1263217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidebar LEGEND, RELICS, AND DENIZENS (page 311) contradicts the Character Creation rules for Legendary Denizens (pg 171)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Specifically page 171 says (non-Scion) Legend 1 Denizens get an innate Purview and Boon, but page 311 makes it sound like they're dependent on Relics for Purviews and it says explicitly they DO NOT get free Boons, exclusively working Marvels via their Relics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T07:58:27-07:00","id":1263354,"title":"","content":"P. 189: 185: &quot;Your character starts in the center of the Virtue track.&quot; 189 does not repeat that information, and it shows an empty virtue track. I propose:<ul><li>Add one dot to the center of the track, to show that this is not a &quot;score&quot;</li> <li>Change the circles in the Virtue track to squares, to indicate that this is something that changes (like a Health or Legend point), instead of a &quot;score&quot; that is constant</li> <li>Add the mark (dot or box) to the center of the Virtue track of each character.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> P. 189: Virtuous condition box<br /> &quot;Effect: Every point of Momentum you spend to augment a roll with a Virtue receives an <i>additional </i>die...&quot; This is the same wording as paragraph 2 under Virtues (same page). What is not clear is how they intersect.<br /> Example: If Eric is at the midline, and he wants to act against his fate, he gets two dice whenever he adds Momentum. This is clear. If he is at 100% Audacity, he is incapable of acting fatalistic. Giving up is no longer something he can even conceive of. But when he continues to act Audaciously, does he get two dice per Momentum (no mechanical change from augmenting a roll normally) or does he get three now (augmenting a roll, <b>plus</b> an extra die because of his Virtuous condition)? This is not clear.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.191 compared to 171: 191 details legendary titles, which &quot;Every Divine character has...&quot; (191). pp. 171 and following (the ready-made characters) do not show any legendary titles. Unless they each have as their first title &quot;Scion of ___,&quot; which doesn't seem to follow rules as written (&quot;Each Calling has a list of associated keywords used to build a character\u2019s Legendary Title....The first Title (for Legend 1) is often related to a character\u2019s Visitation.&quot;). At very least, Emanuel Montero would never call himself a Scion. He is Incarnate!<br /> <br /> If the Legend 1 title of each ready-made character is &quot;Scion of ___&quot;, either 191 needs to detail that the Legend 1 Title is <b>always</b> &quot;Scion of ____&quot; or change a few pregens to different options. (maybe change Emanuel to &quot;Xiuhtechutli Reborn&quot; and Rhiannon to &quot;Master of the Fire Within&quot;?)<br /> <br /> If the authors choose to make the Title a customization (in the same way that the Deeds are blank), I propose that you call out the fact that the Titles are missing (&quot;To give the characters a personal feel, you have space to choose what Legendary Title was given at Visitation. Choose from the options listed, or make your own following the rules on pages 191-195&quot;.), and provide a few suggested titles.<br /> <br /> Also 191-195: Why are there Skills listed with each Calling? I think Failure Deeds need to be actions failed in those Skills, but this is never said in the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T09:22:30-07:00","id":1263366,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Hero pg 223: but a character may only have fve Knacks \u201cactive\u201d at a time, corresponding to their Calling dots, until they gain more by rising in Legend. Immortal Knacks are worth two Calling dots to keep active;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Hero pg 183: while they can learn more, they may only have as many active as they have Calling dots.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Hero pg 191: Each Calling informs the character\u2019s choice of Knacks. Your character can have <i>one </i>Knack active <i>per dot </i>of each Calling, and they must correspond to the specifc Calling dots. They can buy additional Knacks, but may only have as many Knacks active as they have dots of Callings.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Page 183 and 191 do not specify that immortal knacks are worth 2 active knacks at a time, instead imply they are treated equally and active knacks = calling dots irrespective of knack type</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T09:24:39-07:00","id":1263367,"title":"","content":"Hero pg 315 Under Therianthrope: <b><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Feral Hunter: </span></b><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Choose a Heroic or Immortal Hunter </span><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Knack.<br /> - Can this be taken multiple times?<br /> - Does a Heroic Knack taken by Feral Hunter still count as 2 active knacks towards to total number of active knacks? </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T15:42:28-07:00","id":1263429,"title":"","content":"References to Calling Crisis, which apparently isn't a thing:<br /> <br /> Pg 198 - Apprentice Resolve, Balm Resolve<br /> Pg 199 - Boon Companion Resolve, Canary/Martyr Resolve<br /> Pg 200 - Jinx Resolve, Nemesis Resolve, Paramour Resolve, Rival Resolve<br /> Pg 201 - Traitor Resolve, Worshipper/Unrequited Paramour<br /> <br /> Also Scion: Origin, pg 155. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24779-shisumo","name":"Shisumo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T17:10:20-07:00","id":1263440,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>p149 - Persephone\u2019s purviews are separated by slashes rather than commas</li> <li>The character sheets (for the pregen characters) have two bruised health levels and two injured, instead of three bruised one injured</li> <li>Movement dice is on the pregen character sheets, thought it doesn\u2019t seem to be a thing in the rules? Unless it means the rushing dice pool?</li> <li>There are still checkboxes next to skills, though it seems \u201casset skills\u201d is no longer something that requires keeping track of.</li> <li>About half of purviews listed with gods aren\u2019t alphabetized (pantheons vary)</li> <li>p182, 184 - The character creation examples for steps one and seven aren't in sidebars like the rest.</li> <li>P182 - sentence \u201cif you're having trouble encapsulating a good concept, try\u201d has no end.</li> <li>P183 - character creation example implies that callings are based on paths</li> <li>P185 - Is there no experience difference between Heroic and Immortal Knacks?</li> <li>p200 - Paramour references a \u201csoul knack\u201d?</li> <li>P196 - Should specify a *player* character cannot have more fatebinding conditions than their legend (before and after you're talking about SGCs)</li> <li>Most of the fatebindings still mention Crisis of Calling, rather than &quot;Failure Deed&quot;</li> <li>(As does Origin, p153)</li> <li>p197 - The mechanical description of fatebindings (\u201crepresented by a pair of persistent condintions\u2026\u201d) is still under the header of \u201cmultiple fatebindings\u201d</li> <li>p183 - Do you get 5 Calling dots to spend, or 2+1+1? It says the latter, while I believe Neall has clarified the former</li> </ul>Purview/Calling discrepancies:<ul><li>Heimdall has Creator, Guardian, Hunter in Hero, but Guardian, Hunter, Warrior in Origins</li> <li>Freya\u2019s Purviews do not match Origins</li> <li>Tsukiyomi had Stars in Origins</li> <li>Benzaiten has the purview \u201cAnimals\u201d instead of \u201cBeasts\u201d (also in Origin)</li> <li>Origin has Hotei\u2019s purview as \u201cPassion\u201d, Hero shows it as \u201cPassion (Joy)\u201d</li> <li>Artemis does not have \u201cWild\u201d in Origin</li> <li>Hera did not have \u201cPassion (Fidelity)\u201d or Beauty in Origin</li> <li>Sarutahiko has 4 callings</li> <li>Kitchi-Manitou is listed as a god in the Origin reference, and a Primordial in Hero</li> <li>Nana\u2019B\u2019Oozoo\u2019s purviews are in a wonky order, making Wisakedjak\u2019s Water look like a Chaos specialty</li> <li>Ptah did not have Prosperity in the Origin reference</li> <li>Osanyin wasn\u2019t present in the Origins reference</li> <li>Chang\u2019e had Beauty in Origins reference.</li> <li>Prince Nezha had Epic Str. in the Origins reference.</li> <li>Goibniu did not have Health in the Origins reference</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T12:31:11-07:00","id":1263652,"title":"","content":"page 3: Yukiko had never her speak - seems to be missing a verb<br /> page 18: where Quetzalcoatl brought them back life<br /> page 19: became known <u><b>w</b></u>as the<br /> page 19: his ste<u><b>a</b></u>d, Grani<br /> page 20: for every instance of Ganesh riding in on a mouse to welcome his child to the Sh\u00e9n - shouldn't he welcome them to the Dev\u00e1 instead?<br /> page 22: Don't the other structures mentioned here distract you<br /> page 30: The Grandchildren (Yoruba: _m_)<br /> page 46: The second letter of V\u00f6luspa is off<br /> page 46, 47, 51: Text after the word Seidr is italicized<br /> page 46: loving <b><u>flyting</u></b> in the grand halls<br /> page 50: Loki <u><b>felt</b></u> became enraged<br /> page 52 Midgardr is doubled<br /> page 72: He challenged Amaterasu to a du<u><b>a</b></u>l of creation<br /> page 172 - 181: Not all of the Birthrights of the Ready-Made Caharcters are described in detail later in tne book<br /> page 182: The rules say a skill may only be shared between two Paths, not all three - but the Example contradicts it with Sigr\u00fan selecting Occult for all three Paths<br /> page 183: The rules make no mention of possible &quot;Attribute overflow&quot; when your Favorite Approach causes one of your Attributes to rise above 5<br /> page 183: The numerical values given for Sigr\u00fan's Attributes are incorrect - both Manipulation and Composure are too high (should be Manipulation 1 and Composure 3)<br /> page 183: The rules say you get four Calling dots, but the Example implies Sigr\u00fan has five - it doesn't mention her dots, but she chooses five Knacks, and the Ready-Made Characters likewise have five Calling dots<br /> page 183: It's not readily apparent that Hunter is the third Calling chosen for Sigr\u00fan in the Example, it's only implied via the chosen Knacks<br /> page 184: The Example for Step Seven is not boxed in like the rest of the Examples<br /> page 191: The text mentions a fixed distribution of 2-2-1 for Calling dots, when four of the Ready-Made Caharcters use 3-1-1 instead<br /> page 217: The layout for Giantsbane is off - with only the name at the bottom at the left column it can be easy to overlook<br /> page 237: The entry under Pantheon Motifs lists Amatsukami when they are referred to as Kami throughout the rest of the book<br /> page 238: The text color of the example for Offscreen Action doesn't match the other examples<br /> page 240: despite their <u><b>full</b></u> hearts full of wanderlust<br /> page 243/244: In the example for Chaos, the character is named Maeve Whelan in the beginning and Michal at the end<br /> page 247: The name of Heavenly Stride has a differing layout, which makes it easy to overlook<br /> page 247: The Cost entry for Unerring Flight simply says 1 Legend. Spend or Imbue?<br /> page 253, 254, 255, 257, 263: The Cost entry for some Boons (Fateful Connection, Glacial Pace, Enchanting Evening, Phase Cloak, Tugging at Heartstrings and Reborn in the Depths) has a differing layout<br /> page 257: They something without realizing it - seems to be missing a verb<br /> page 264: The layout of Wyrd's example doesn't match the other purview examples<br /> page 276: Should Igbo \u00e8z\u00e8 be bolded like kishotenketsu?<br /> page 316: two of the bullet points under Glimpses forward are in italics, the other two aren't<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24456-xizzillix","user":"Xizzillix","date":". 10-31-2018, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24456-xizzillix","name":"Xizzillix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T18:38:59-07:00","id":1263717,"title":"","content":"Page 247 Heavenly Stride lacks the formatting of the other Boons","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":". 10-30-2018, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T12:36:44-07:00","id":1264099,"title":"","content":"The 'Terrible to Behold' SIdebar on page 242 mentions that a God or Scion with the appropriate Title can emulate Boons as Marvels of a different Purview at no additional cost. Only, the Marvels section only has a single cost list for duplicating Boons, no mater which Purview they fall under. So this part probably needs some clarification if any kind of cost difference is expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T17:51:17-07:00","id":1264163,"title":"","content":"Page 13 - it seems notable how often notable appears in this sentence...<br /> <br /> Notable for a very notable touch of the Rashomon Effect, where Hercules realizes that he doesn\u2019t actually remem-ber his history, but that it doesn\u2019t actually matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24742-seguin","name":"seguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T08:07:58-07:00","id":1264272,"title":"","content":"Page 194 - The Liminal Calling lists Manipulation as one of its skills. There is no such skill, Manipulation is an attribute. Was it supposed to be subterfuge?<br /> <br /> Page 183 - The example for Attributes make a couple of mistakes. It gives one of the Mental attribute points to Composure, a social attribute. It should instead go to Resolve. At the final attribute scores at the end of the example, Manipulation and Composure each have one dot too many. Manipulation should be at 1 and Composure (assuming the earlier mix up with Resolve is fixed) should be at 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","name":"baboonking","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2030_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T08:19:14-07:00","id":1264276,"title":"","content":"Not sure if missing images/pictures, like the ones at pages 122-123 and 184, counts as errata. But I'll mention it here just in case.<br /> <br /> I also assume the black circle in all the character creation examples is supposed to have some kind of picture in the final version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","name":"baboonking","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2030_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T13:44:54-07:00","id":1264327,"title":"","content":"Below is the address to a Google doc of what I managed to find for Errata (didn't want to flood the forum). It also includes a master list of &quot;Pg. XX&quot; appearances<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OsTeLAyKzBHreyBPy1EKRFlTVlZ2-v2qBPV5-UeAWeU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OsTeLAyKzBHreyBPy1EKRFlTVlZ2-v2qBPV5-UeAWeU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OsTeLAyKzBHreyBPy1EKRFlTVlZ2-v2qBPV5-UeAWeU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OsTeLAyKzBHreyBPy1EKRFlTVlZ2-v2qBPV5-UeAWeU/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24741-irishspitfyre","name":"irishspitfyre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T16:31:16-07:00","id":1264346,"title":"","content":"P.g. 236 Tempered Knack:<br /> Tempered: When you wear no armor, you are considered to have the Armored Tag. This benefit stacks with the increased difficulty of the inflict damage Stunt granted by any other armor you wear when you fight lesser foes (minor characters, or anyone a Tier lower than you). <br /> 1. Which armoured tag does the player get? This is the only place that Armoured Tag is referenced on its own, I assume it means increase the difficulty of Inflict damage by 1 but its not very clear. <br /> 2. How can the knack stack with worn armour when the knack only works when you have no armour? This seems to not work. <br /> Issue is also present in Origin, but knack has the name &quot;Well-Tempered&quot; there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T02:28:33-07:00","id":1264398,"title":"","content":"On page 171 the box &quot;Visitations and Origin Characters&quot; has the wrong step numbers. For example, it lists choosing Purviews as Step 6, when it's actually Step 7. A quick run through that and double-checking of the step numbers should fix it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T05:59:07-07:00","id":1264417,"title":"","content":"The Fatebinding Conditions reference &quot;Narrative Advantage&quot; (Worshipper) and &quot;Narrative Disadvantage&quot; (Jinx). The capitalisation makes it seem like a defined term, but they show up nowhere else (besides &quot;narrative advantage&quot; in the Palace of Memory knack.) I assume they are old terms for Twist of Fate and consequences for overinvoking your paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24080-cybertier","name":"cybertier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T09:21:31-07:00","id":1264441,"title":"","content":"Not strictly Errata but I checked with Neall before posting: Lakshmi shouldn't have Wild. Fertility adequately covers her plant associations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T13:18:16-08:00","id":1264786,"title":"","content":"page 72: Tsukiyomi's Alias is written Tsukiyomi-<b>m</b>o-Mikoto when other Kami have -no- in the middle. And his description begins with another misspelling of his name: Tsukiyom<b>o</b><br /> page 75: Sarutahiko has four Callings listed<br /> page 77: while he tells them stories and gives them sweets to make them smile<b>s</b>.<br /> page 72: Hotei, the <b>Seven</b> Fortune of Joy<br /> page 82: As much a<b>s</b> term for the spirits<br /> page 83: Some have adamantly argued that <b>there</b> she has<br /> Page 84: Winonah continues to <b>be</b> exist in the World","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24456-xizzillix","name":"Xizzillix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T11:28:42-08:00","id":1266462,"title":"","content":"Page 211: &quot;Reduce one tag\u2019s numerical value by one or remove one effect at the end of each scene in which<br /> Relic was used as intended without its user fulfilling a Virtue; restore to full functionality as soon<br /> as user fulfills a Virtue while using it.&quot; Is written as both a 2-dot and 3-dot flaw","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23677-the-eternal-keeper","name":"The Eternal Keeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T19:22:29-08:00","id":1266578,"title":"","content":"The Titanspawn template (pg 287) references Size or Segment rules that don't seem to be in the book. Segments come up again in the Seamonsters sidebar (pg 296.) I don't know if these were supposed to be in Hero or Origin (where the monster template also references them,) but figured it was worth noting here just in case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":